			"notes": "## Umbra Client 1.4.0 — Menu & ESP\n\n### New Menu (INSERT or DELETE)\n\nThe old ClickGUI and the flat menu have been replaced with a new menu. Both keys now open the same interface:\n\n* **CATEGORIES** sidebar with collapsible groups, module counts, and quick-jump rows\n* **FEATURES** panel where modules can be expanded and settings changed directly\n* Toggles, sliders, dropdowns, and click-to-bind keybinds\n* Tooltips for modules and settings\n* Search bar at the top\n* Config Save/Load buttons\n\n### New Config System\n\nSettings are now stored in:\n\n`Documents/Umbra/configs`\n\nConfigs use human-readable `.ucfg` files (JSON).\n\n* `default.ucfg` is created automatically on first launch\n* Old settings from `.minecraft/umbra` are no longer used\n* This means you'll need to set everything up again after updating\n\n### Rust-style EntityESP\n\nEntityESP has been reworked with a Rust-style look:\n\n* 2D corner box or full box\n* Name\n* Distance\n* Health bar\n* Held item with text and icon\n* Flags for **SNEAK, ELYTRA, EATING, PEARL, BOW**\n* Optional 3D boxes\n* Optional chams/model fill\n* Adjustable max distance\n\n### PvP Changes\n\nAutoClicker, Aimbot, and TriggerBot now have a **\"Only/Require Weapon\"** option for swords and axes.\n\nAimbot still uses the same legit hold-to-aim behavior by default.\n\n### Install\n\nReplace your old jar with:\n\n`Umbra-1.4.0.jar`\n\n**Note:** The old settings won't be carried over because of the new config system."
		},
